#{[17592186410469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186410464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410469 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5db94061-cdf0-57e7-b013-67cd72f1cc89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410471 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410471 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410471 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410471 #edb/ref 1071 "Two fair  four-sided dice are rolled and $X$ is the absolute difference of their scores. The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{SD}[X]?$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ddfb506-4076-564a-9cbf-01888893404d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410471 #edb/ref 1074 "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{25}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410473 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410473 #edb/ref 1069 "q-84011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410473 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410473 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{5}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{3}{4},$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410473 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9682caf0-f7aa-52f6-bd4c-fbe55d6bcce7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410473 #edb/ref 1074 "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{3}{4}-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{100}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410475 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410475 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b426a90-801f-55fb-8b5f-1d3d9be30906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410475 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410476 #edb/ref 1058