db/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418082 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "735318e8-b065-526f-8046-9b9ea9da16fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418083 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9520dcff-aa35-56e0-9ddc-bd7600942c23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418084 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418084 #edb/ref 1069 "q-84199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418084 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418084 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $X$ be the outcome of rolling an unfair  six-sided die that follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418084 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "098ae999-41d1-5d21-93d9-672720b112c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418084 #edb/ref 1074 "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8})+5(\\frac{1}{16})+6(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+4(\\frac{3}{8})+9(\\frac{1}{4})+16(\\frac{1}{8})+25(\\frac{1}{16})+36(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}-{(\\frac{45}{16})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}-\\frac{2025}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{455}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418085 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418085 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418085 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418085 #edb/ref 1071 "Two fair  four-sided dice are rolled and $X$ is the absolute difference of their scores. The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{2}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418085 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b04f202f-7340-5122-b2d5-59ca0d357302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418085 #edb/ref 1074 "The variance of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{2}{8})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{2}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4}$ into the variance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{(x-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the variance as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & ={(0-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{(1-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(2-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(3-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{(-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(\\frac{7}{4})}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =(\\frac{25}{16})(\\frac{2}{8})+(\\frac{1}{16})(\\frac{3}{8})+(\\frac{9}{16})(\\frac{2}{8})+(\\frac{49}{16})(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
